CM_ "Inferred from a 39.142-second CAN capture. Button identities follow the supplied action order. Unidentified traffic is omitted. User specifies a 0..5 V potentiometer signal. Scaling assumes 4095 counts equals 5 V; exact ADC resolution and calibration are not independently verified.";
CM_ BO_ 272 "Standard CAN ID 0x110; nominal 10 ms period.";
CM_ SG_ 272 Potentiometer "Unsigned big-endian upper 12 bits of the two-byte payload: (byte0 << 4) | (byte1 >> 4). Low nibble of byte1 was always zero. Voltage = raw * 5 / 4095, assuming 12-bit full-scale conversion. Observed raw range 182..4095 decodes to approximately 0.2222..5 V. Captured minimum is not offset-corrected to zero.";
CM_ SG_ 577 Button1 "Byte 0 bit 7, active high. Press intervals approximately 4.480..5.620 s and 6.430..7.230 s relative to first captured frame.";
CM_ SG_ 608 Button2 "Byte 0 bit 7, active high. Press intervals approximately 9.841..10.851 s and 11.911..13.011 s relative to first captured frame.";
CM_ BO_ 1024 "Standard CAN ID 0x400; nominal 50 ms period. All three bytes repeat exactly every 64 frames (3.2 s) in this capture. Demo waveform identities supplied by user; controllability is not verified.";
CM_ SG_ 1024 SquareWave "Byte 0 preserved as unsigned raw data. Observed 0x00 and 0xFF plateaus plus one 0x80 sample per 64-frame cycle. Physical units and intended signedness are unverified.";
CM_ SG_ 1024 Sawtooth "Byte 1, unsigned. Increments by 4 modulo 256 each frame; observed range 0..252.";
CM_ SG_ 1024 SineWave "Byte 2 interpreted as signed two's-complement. Observed smooth sine-like waveform spanning -127..127. Physical units unspecified.";

